From: Surface Overdrive <noreply@surface-overdrive>
Subject: [PATCH] ipu3: hardware temporal denoise (TNR3) in still scenes; only the chosen picture size and bigger

The ImgU has a temporal noise reduction (TNR3) that the kernel leaves at a feedback of 0. NoiseReduction now sets it from the
tuning data (tnr3 in good light, tnr3Dark in the dark, interpolated from exposure x gain like the software filter) and the
live profile ("tnr3"). Front camera, 2560x1920, bright room: temporal noise of still areas 1.27 -> 0.80, chroma 0.90 -> 0.56
at a feedback of 1024, at no cost to the processor.

TNR3 cannot tell motion from noise: moving hands and heads left banded ghosts. The feedback therefore follows the motion of
the scene, judged from the 3A grid (green average of every cell against the previous frame at the same overall brightness,
since the auto exposure changes the whole picture a little all the time): off at once when over 2.5% of the cells move, back
after four still frames, by 8% a frame. In the dark the front camera's tuning leaves TNR3 off: the ghosts were worst there
and the software filter already takes the grain of still areas to almost nothing.

The sizes offered start at the size chosen in the Cameras page: applications without wishes (Kamoso, GStreamer) take the
size closest to 640x480 whatever comes first, so a smaller size on offer took Kamoso's pictures down to it.

---
diff -ruN a/src/ipa/ipu3/algorithms/noise_reduction.cpp b/src/ipa/ipu3/algorithms/noise_reduction.cpp
--- a/src/ipa/ipu3/algorithms/noise_reduction.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/ipu3/algorithms/noise_reduction.cpp
@@ -42,7 +42,22 @@
  *   xnr3: [ alpha y0, u0, v0, ydiff, udiff, vdiff, coring u0, v0, udiff, vdiff, blending strength ]
  *   xnr3Binned: the same for the 2x2 binned sensor modes
  *   chnr: [ coring u, v, sense gain vy, vu, vv, hy, hu, hv, FIR tap 0, 1, 2, IIR weight ]
- * The "xnr3" and "chnr" keys of the camera's live profile win over the tuning data (to tune on a running camera).
+ *   tnr3: [ max feedback Y, max feedback U/V, knee Y1, knee Y2, sigma, slope, rounding ]
+ *   tnr3Dark: the same in the dark; the values in between follow the light
+ * The "xnr3", "chnr" and "tnr3" keys of the camera's live profile win over the tuning data (to tune on a running camera).
+ *
+ * TNR3 is the ImgU's temporal noise reduction: each output frame is blended with the previous one in the hardware, at no
+ * cost to the processor. The kernel leaves its feedback at 0 (off). Measured on the Surface Go's front camera
+ * (2026-10-29, 2560x1920 in a bright room): with a max feedback of 1024 the temporal noise of still areas fell from 1.81
+ * to 1.04 and the chroma noise from 0.96 to 0.59, at 1536 to 0.69 and 0.38; moving edges leave a faint trail that grows
+ * with the feedback, and from about 1900 the picture freezes (2048 is full feedback). The rest of the values as the
+ * kernel computes them (knees 768 and 1280, sigma 256, slope and rounding 0).
+ *
+ * TNR3 has no motion detection worth the name: at a strong feedback a moving head left banded ghosts behind it, whatever
+ * its sigma. So the feedback follows the motion of the scene, judged from the 3A statistics of each frame (the green
+ * average of every cell of the grid against the previous frame): it drops to nothing as soon as the scene moves, and
+ * comes back over about half a second once it is still again. Still scenes get the full strength, moving ones none
+ * (and motion blur hides the grain there anyway).
  */
 
 namespace {
@@ -81,6 +96,9 @@
 /* What the kernel sets when it computes the parameters itself (drivers/staging/media/ipu3). */
 constexpr std::array<double, 11> kXnr3Off = { 2047, 2047, 2047, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0 };
 constexpr std::array<double, 12> kChnrDefault = { 0, 0, 6, 6, 6, 4, 4, 4, 8, 12, 0, 129 };
+constexpr std::array<double, 7> kTnr3Off = { 0, 0, 768, 1280, 256, 0, 0 };
+/* the feedback never reaches the point where the picture freezes */
+constexpr double kTnr3MaxFeedback = 1800;
 
 } /* namespace */
 
@@ -89,6 +107,8 @@
 	hasXnr3_ = readList(tuningData, "xnr3", xnr3_);
 	hasXnr3Binned_ = readList(tuningData, "xnr3Binned", xnr3Binned_);
 	hasChnr_ = readList(tuningData, "chnr", chnr_);
+	hasTnr3_ = readList(tuningData, "tnr3", tnr3_);
+	hasTnr3Dark_ = readList(tuningData, "tnr3Dark", tnr3Dark_);
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -101,10 +121,14 @@
 	/* A new streaming session: the kernel starts from its own values again. */
 	xnr3Set_ = false;
 	chnrSet_ = false;
+	tnr3Set_ = false;
+	tnr3Still_ = 0.0;
+	stillFrames_ = 0;
+	prevCells_.clear();
 	return 0;
 }
 
-void NoiseReduction::prepare([[maybe_unused]] IPAContext &context, [[maybe_unused]] const uint32_t frame,
+void NoiseReduction::prepare(IPAContext &context, [[maybe_unused]] const uint32_t frame,
 			     [[maybe_unused]] IPAFrameContext &frameContext, ipu3_uapi_params *params)
 {
 	if (profile_)
@@ -133,6 +157,47 @@
 		xnr3Set_ = hasX;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * TNR3: the strength follows the light like the software filter of the pipeline handler, from the exposure time x
+	 * gain the auto exposure set: 8 ms at gain 1 and less is good light, 40 ms at gain 1 and more the dark.
+	 */
+	std::array<double, kTnr3Size> n = tnr3_;
+	bool hasN = hasTnr3_;
+	if (hasTnr3_ && hasTnr3Dark_) {
+		const auto &agc = context.activeState.agc;
+		const double light = agc.exposure * context.configuration.sensor.lineDuration.get<std::micro>() * agc.gain;
+		const double dark = std::clamp((light - 8000.0) / (40000.0 - 8000.0), 0.0, 1.0);
+		for (unsigned int i = 0; i < kTnr3Size; i++)
+			n[i] = tnr3_[i] + dark * (tnr3Dark_[i] - tnr3_[i]);
+	}
+	if (profileList(profile_.get(), "tnr3", n))
+		hasN = true;
+	n[0] *= tnr3Still_;
+	n[1] *= tnr3Still_;
+	if (!hasN && tnr3Set_)
+		n = kTnr3Off;
+	if (hasN || tnr3Set_) {
+		ipu3_uapi_isp_tnr3_params &t = params->tnr3_dmem_params;
+		t = {};
+		t.maxfb_y = clampU(std::min(n[0], kTnr3MaxFeedback), 0xffff);
+		t.maxfb_u = clampU(std::min(n[1], kTnr3MaxFeedback), 0xffff);
+		t.maxfb_v = t.maxfb_u;
+		t.knee_y1 = clampU(n[2], 0xffff);
+		t.knee_y2 = clampU(n[3], 0xffff);
+		t.round_adj_y = clampU(n[6], 0xffff);
+		t.round_adj_u = t.round_adj_y;
+		t.round_adj_v = t.round_adj_y;
+		params->use.tnr3_dmem_params = 1;
+		ipu3_uapi_isp_tnr3_vmem_params &v = params->tnr3_vmem_params;
+		v = {};
+		for (unsigned int i = 0; i < IPU3_UAPI_ISP_TNR3_VMEM_LEN; i++) {
+			v.sigma[i] = clampU(n[4], 0xffff);
+			v.slope[i] = clampU(n[5], 0xffff);
+		}
+		params->use.tnr3_vmem_params = 1;
+		tnr3Set_ = hasN;
+	}
+
 	std::array<double, kChnrSize> c = chnr_;
 	bool hasC = hasChnr_;
 	if (profileList(profile_.get(), "chnr", c))
@@ -161,6 +226,61 @@
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * How still the scene is, from the green average of every cell of the 3A grid against the previous frame: the share of
+ * cells that changed by more than noise does (6% of their value, at least 8 levels). Over 2.5% of moving cells is
+ * a moving scene: the TNR3 feedback goes to nothing at once, and comes back after four still frames, by 8% a frame.
+ */
+void NoiseReduction::process(IPAContext &context, [[maybe_unused]] const uint32_t frame,
+			     [[maybe_unused]] IPAFrameContext &frameContext,
+			     const ipu3_uapi_stats_3a *stats,
+			     [[maybe_unused]] ControlList &metadata)
+{
+	const ipu3_uapi_grid_config &grid = context.configuration.grid.bdsGrid;
+	const uint32_t stride = context.configuration.grid.stride;
+	std::vector<uint32_t> cells;
+	cells.reserve(static_cast<size_t>(grid.width) * grid.height);
+	for (uint32_t y = 0; y < grid.height; y++) {
+		for (uint32_t x = 0; x < grid.width; x++) {
+			const auto *cell = reinterpret_cast<const ipu3_uapi_awb_set_item *>(
+				&stats->awb_raw_buffer.meta_data[y * stride + x]);
+			cells.push_back(static_cast<uint32_t>(cell->Gr_avg) + cell->Gb_avg);
+		}
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * Each frame is compared with the previous one at the same overall brightness: the auto exposure changes the whole
+	 * picture a little from frame to frame (much more in low light), which counted every cell as moving.
+	 */
+	double moving = 1.0;
+	if (prevCells_.size() == cells.size() && !cells.empty()) {
+		double sumA = 0, sumB = 0;
+		for (size_t k = 0; k < cells.size(); k++) {
+			sumA += cells[k];
+			sumB += prevCells_[k];
+		}
+		const double scale = sumA > 0 ? sumB / sumA : 1.0;
+		unsigned int changed = 0;
+		for (size_t k = 0; k < cells.size(); k++) {
+			const double a = cells[k] * scale, b = prevCells_[k];
+			if (std::abs(a - b) > std::max(8.0, 0.06 * std::max(a, b)))
+				changed++;
+		}
+		moving = static_cast<double>(changed) / cells.size();
+	}
+	prevCells_ = std::move(cells);
+
+	/* off at once when the scene moves; back only after a few still frames, then over half a second */
+	if (moving > 0.025) {
+		tnr3Still_ = 0.0;
+		stillFrames_ = 0;
+	} else if (++stillFrames_ >= 4) {
+		tnr3Still_ = std::min(1.0, tnr3Still_ + 0.08);
+	}
+
+	LOG(IPU3NoiseReduction, Debug) << "moving cells " << moving << ", TNR3 strength " << tnr3Still_;
+}
+
 REGISTER_IPA_ALGORITHM(NoiseReduction, "NoiseReduction")
 
 } /* namespace ipa::ipu3::algorithms */
